WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:50.633 --> 00:52.969
A caged lion isn't intimidating.

00:54.387 --> 00:55.555
I can make fun of its whiskers

00:56.473 --> 00:58.433
or call it old or whatever.

00:59.809 --> 01:01.061
Until now,

01:02.479 --> 01:03.855
I've treated movies like a caged lion.

01:07.025 --> 01:07.859
But now,

01:08.693 --> 01:10.570
it's time to face the lion.

01:12.572 --> 01:14.491
I either have to run for my life…

01:19.204 --> 01:20.038
or…

01:23.083 --> 01:24.667
face it head-on.

02:11.923 --> 02:13.049
I'm good.

02:13.133 --> 02:14.384
Just take it.

02:21.766 --> 02:22.600
I read the revision.

02:24.811 --> 02:25.728
You did a good job.

02:27.605 --> 02:29.899
I was hoping to see you fail completely.

02:31.109 --> 02:32.485
Why the hell did you write so well?

02:33.403 --> 02:34.237
Now I'm tempted.

02:38.700 --> 02:39.534
It's good?

02:45.415 --> 02:46.499
Hello.

02:48.084 --> 02:49.460
You're here early.

02:49.544 --> 02:52.380
We had to obtain
his award declination form first.

02:52.463 --> 02:53.339
Of course.

02:54.716 --> 02:55.550
Hello.

02:56.217 --> 02:57.218
Make sure you succeed.

02:58.887 --> 03:00.638
You betrayed me and left,

03:01.264 --> 03:02.348
so if you fail, you're done.

03:14.402 --> 03:16.654
We'll handle those separately.

03:16.738 --> 03:18.364
Clause 5 is important.

03:18.448 --> 03:20.575
"The right to create derivative works."

03:20.658 --> 03:24.120
Derivative works include
spin-offs or merchandise.

03:24.203 --> 03:26.706
Now, please enter your address
and everything else.

03:26.789 --> 03:28.207
WRITER'S NAME: HWANG DONG-MAN

03:28.291 --> 03:29.667
FILM PRODUCTION COMPANY:
KOPARK FILM PRODUCTION

03:31.794 --> 03:33.671
All right, let's take a photo.

03:33.755 --> 03:34.589
Director Hwang?

03:34.672 --> 03:36.841
Smile and say cheese.

03:36.925 --> 03:37.759
Cheese.

03:38.217 --> 03:39.135
Cheese.

03:40.678 --> 03:41.763
Congratulations.

03:41.846 --> 03:43.723
Contracts are freaking scary.

03:44.390 --> 03:45.725
If I don't finish this,

03:45.808 --> 03:48.853
I'll be liable
unless there's a natural disaster.

03:49.520 --> 03:51.522
That's just typical contract language.

03:52.607 --> 03:53.900
This is the beginning.

03:55.526 --> 03:57.320
I'll call you later.

03:57.403 --> 03:58.738
-I'm looking forward to it.
-Thank you.

04:01.366 --> 04:03.660
You'll probably get
a few plagiarism accusations.

04:03.743 --> 04:06.037
It's a story about AI and weather,

04:06.120 --> 04:08.581
and that alone guarantees
someone will claim it as theirs.

04:09.540 --> 04:10.792
Don't be scared.

04:11.376 --> 04:12.794
There are a lot of people

04:12.877 --> 04:15.922
who mistakenly think
they're the only ones with ideas.

04:16.506 --> 04:20.093
Just to be safe, were you involved in any
harassment issues that could resurface?

04:20.802 --> 04:22.345
-Come on.
-School bullying?

04:22.428 --> 04:23.972
I was the one who got beaten up.

04:24.055 --> 04:26.266
If a scandal breaks out
after all that effort,

04:26.349 --> 04:28.309
it could be scrapped and not get released.

04:29.102 --> 04:32.021
Delete everything you posted online,
including social media.

04:32.105 --> 04:34.440
Don't think about what might be
problematic or not. Just delete it all.

04:35.066 --> 04:37.694
Not a single person in this world
wants you to succeed.

04:38.695 --> 04:39.696
Except your parents.

04:41.531 --> 04:44.867
You used to cheer for others to fail
when their films got greenlit,

04:44.951 --> 04:47.245
so people like the old you
will come at you,

04:47.328 --> 04:48.830
hoping you fail.

04:50.957 --> 04:52.792
Let's revise one detail in the screenplay.

04:53.418 --> 04:57.672
If you want the evil protagonist
to suddenly turn good and make it work,

04:57.755 --> 04:59.507
he has to be truly evil at the start.

04:59.590 --> 05:02.427
Talking tough and yelling
doesn't make you scary.

05:03.886 --> 05:05.179
It feels like

05:05.763 --> 05:07.056
something is missing.

05:08.266 --> 05:09.475
A certain element of evil.

05:11.519 --> 05:13.688
Work on that so we can start casting.

05:14.480 --> 05:15.940
Who's your top choice?

05:17.233 --> 05:18.067
They're here.

05:19.235 --> 05:20.278
Hey.

05:20.361 --> 05:21.195
There you are.

05:22.447 --> 05:23.656
Come inside. It's cold.

05:25.825 --> 05:26.868
Hey.

05:27.785 --> 05:29.787
Hey, looking good.

05:31.873 --> 05:33.499
People like the old me.

05:39.047 --> 05:41.674
-Congratulations!
-Congrats, Hwang Dong-man!

05:42.467 --> 05:43.968
This year's winner!

05:45.178 --> 05:46.429
-Hwang Dong-man!
-Hwang Dong-man!

05:46.512 --> 05:49.015
-Hwang Dong-man!
-Hwang Dong-man!

05:49.098 --> 05:50.099
Jeez!

05:50.183 --> 05:51.601
Congratulations, my foot.

05:51.684 --> 05:53.436
I just picked up the winner's leftovers.

05:53.519 --> 05:54.604
Congrats, man!

05:54.687 --> 05:56.689
Hey, it's not easy to pick up leftovers.

05:56.773 --> 05:57.774
You can't beat luck!

05:57.857 --> 05:59.233
Not even talented people can--

06:03.488 --> 06:05.156
-Goodness gracious.
-Just come in.

06:08.701 --> 06:09.702
Hey, Dong-man.

06:09.786 --> 06:11.329
-Yeah?
-Eat up, okay?

06:11.954 --> 06:13.456
-Okay.
-Here, have this too.

06:14.082 --> 06:15.166
That's enough.

06:15.249 --> 06:18.044
It feels like I'm sending a son
to the military.

06:19.087 --> 06:20.129
Why am I getting so emotional?

06:21.130 --> 06:23.716
I wanted Dong-man to grow up carefree

06:23.800 --> 06:25.843
and never experience
anything ugly and harsh,

06:25.927 --> 06:28.429
but knowing you'll go through what I did

06:28.513 --> 06:29.680
makes me feel uneasy.

06:29.764 --> 06:31.599
You have to lead 200 people

06:31.682 --> 06:33.142
who won't listen for shit,

06:33.226 --> 06:35.353
and there are always
a few sour faces on set.

06:35.436 --> 06:37.313
Not a single scene goes as planned,

06:37.396 --> 06:39.982
and you stress over
whether you're blowing 20 billion won

06:40.066 --> 06:42.235
or ruining an actor's future.

06:43.194 --> 06:46.531
You'll consider running away hundreds,
maybe thousands of times.

06:47.406 --> 06:49.742
You're stressed
because you want to do well.

06:49.826 --> 06:52.787
I'm telling you,
I have zero desire to succeed.

06:52.870 --> 06:56.415
I'm going to fail completely
and talk about it for the rest of my life.

06:56.499 --> 06:58.251
Hey, you think it's easy to fail?

06:58.835 --> 07:00.628
You can only call it a hit or flop
if you finish it.

07:00.711 --> 07:02.171
Just leave him be.

07:02.255 --> 07:05.716
Whether he hears military stories or not,
he won't know until he goes through it.

07:08.219 --> 07:10.179
-Here's some more food.
-Hey.

07:10.263 --> 07:11.973
Why are you bringing so much?

07:12.056 --> 07:12.890
You don't have to.

07:12.974 --> 07:14.308
Because it's a good day.

07:14.976 --> 07:17.145
Think of it as your last meal.

07:17.228 --> 07:18.896
From now on,

07:19.564 --> 07:21.149
anything you eat won't taste good.

07:22.650 --> 07:25.278
I've never experienced losing my appetite

07:25.903 --> 07:27.113
or having trouble sleeping.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.448
I don't know what that feels like.

07:29.782 --> 07:31.659
You'll know soon enough.

07:35.663 --> 07:38.249
When I was shooting my debut film,

07:38.332 --> 07:40.710
I prayed for the first time in my life.

07:40.793 --> 07:43.629
"I don't care about success.
Just let me finish this,

07:43.713 --> 07:45.965
and I'll never turn my back on you."

07:47.592 --> 07:49.552
I still go to church to this day.

07:50.553 --> 07:55.224
I knew I couldn't quit on my own,
even if I tried, and wondered,

07:55.308 --> 07:58.227
"How badly do I have to get hurt
to be pulled from the film?"

07:58.311 --> 08:01.022
"I wish the Grim Reaper
would come and get me."

08:07.320 --> 08:08.154
Hey.

08:10.072 --> 08:11.032
Just hang in there.

08:11.866 --> 08:12.700
Got it?

08:13.451 --> 08:15.828
Think of it as serving in the military
without the haircut.

08:15.912 --> 08:17.121
A year and a half, right?

08:18.581 --> 08:19.749
That time will pass somehow.

08:20.791 --> 08:22.084
Do you remember?

08:23.002 --> 08:24.670
When you were shooting that film,

08:24.754 --> 08:28.382
you called me in the middle of the night
and just sobbed without saying a word.

08:29.133 --> 08:31.177
-I did?
-You said one word.

08:32.178 --> 08:33.846
"Dong-man…"

08:36.807 --> 08:38.059
I thought you were howling.

08:51.822 --> 08:53.950
We need to push Hwang Dong-man
to his limits.

08:54.033 --> 08:57.495
He can either tremble in fear,
give up, and fall flat on his face,

08:57.578 --> 09:00.122
or he can stand up
and make something of himself.

09:00.206 --> 09:02.250
We need to push his limits either way.

09:02.833 --> 09:05.253
Do you want to spend your whole life
letting him piss you off?

09:06.254 --> 09:07.838
You can't spend
government funds like that.

09:07.922 --> 09:10.091
That's exactly what it's for.

09:10.174 --> 09:12.760
It's to help people
who keep falling short,

09:14.095 --> 09:17.014
not to help people
who are already doing well.

09:20.226 --> 09:21.352
How many episodes have you written so far?

09:23.563 --> 09:25.106
Damn it.

09:30.319 --> 09:33.155
We have to send over
the first two episodes next week.

09:42.957 --> 09:44.000
Damn it.

09:53.301 --> 09:54.385
Come eat.

10:15.239 --> 10:17.074
BIG HYPE, NO SUBSTANCE
THE CAST WENT THROUGH HELL FOR THIS MOVIE

10:17.158 --> 10:18.492
THIS COMMENT HAS BEEN DELETED

10:20.244 --> 10:22.121
THIS COMMENT HAS BEEN DELETED

10:25.249 --> 10:26.751
EXPOSING CHOI FILM'S EXPLOITATION
OF SMALL, POWERLESS PRODUCTION COMPANIES

10:26.834 --> 10:28.377
THIS POST HAS BEEN DELETED

10:35.801 --> 10:38.304
I urgently need 1.7 million won
for my cat's treatment.

10:38.387 --> 10:40.181
Are there any decent loan sharks?

10:40.264 --> 10:41.891
There's no such thing
as "decent loan sharks."

10:41.974 --> 10:44.685
Loan sharks copy the entire contact list
on your phone.

10:44.769 --> 10:46.979
If you don't pay them back,
they press your acquaintances.

10:47.063 --> 10:48.230
You're basically asking for humiliation.

10:50.816 --> 10:54.487
If you don't pay the interest on time
or try to ghost me,

10:54.570 --> 10:58.074
I'll collect what you owe
from everyone in your phone.

10:58.157 --> 11:00.826
Don't forget I have your contact list.

11:00.910 --> 11:04.163
And don't even think about
going to the cops over illegal lending.

11:05.164 --> 11:05.998
Here.

11:07.208 --> 11:08.125
Hey.

11:08.751 --> 11:09.627
Excuse me.

11:10.628 --> 11:12.046
If I repay you in full today,

11:12.755 --> 11:14.131
how much would it be?

11:18.594 --> 11:19.553
I borrowed 1.7 million won

11:19.637 --> 11:21.472
and paid over five million
just in interest so far,

11:21.555 --> 11:23.724
so how can my balance be 11 million won?

11:25.101 --> 11:26.602
No, that's not what I'm saying.

11:32.775 --> 11:33.734
Looks like this bastard

11:34.443 --> 11:35.569
came into some money.

11:36.195 --> 11:37.071
Well, shit.

11:38.155 --> 11:40.157
When can I sign the director's contract?

11:40.241 --> 11:43.452
We have to return the funds we got
for Knock knock knock

11:43.536 --> 11:45.913
and receive them again for Weather Maker,

11:45.996 --> 11:47.998
so it'll take about ten days.

11:48.082 --> 11:48.916
Why?

11:49.792 --> 11:51.127
Did something come up?

11:51.919 --> 11:53.379
No, ten days is…

11:55.548 --> 11:57.049
It's fine.

11:57.133 --> 11:59.009
It's not important. Don't worry about it.

11:59.093 --> 12:00.094
Talk to you later.

12:05.141 --> 12:07.143
It's 11.3 million won if you pay tonight

12:07.226 --> 12:08.602
and 11.6 million won if you pay tomorrow.

12:08.686 --> 12:10.896
It goes up 300,000 won a day,

12:10.980 --> 12:12.690
so send me the damn money.

12:39.467 --> 12:40.551
Did you borrow from a loan shark?

12:44.638 --> 12:45.473
Why?

12:47.850 --> 12:49.226
-Tell me.
-Stay out of it.

12:50.728 --> 12:52.563
I told you my film got greenlit.

12:53.439 --> 12:54.982
Don't try my patience.

12:55.065 --> 12:57.067
My head's about to explode as it is.

13:01.280 --> 13:02.198
What's your purpose?

13:04.658 --> 13:05.659
Say your film turns out well.

13:06.243 --> 13:07.077
Will it redeem you?

13:08.078 --> 13:09.079
Say your film turns out well.

13:09.705 --> 13:10.789
Will it save the country?

13:10.873 --> 13:12.041
I'll be less embarrassing!

13:12.124 --> 13:13.959
Your purpose in life
is to be less embarrassing?

13:14.043 --> 13:15.085
Yeah!

13:15.169 --> 13:16.921
I'm so embarrassed by who I am right now

13:17.004 --> 13:19.006
that becoming
a slightly less embarrassing person

13:19.089 --> 13:20.674
is my purpose in life!

13:20.758 --> 13:23.177
I don't know about any ultimate purpose,
and I don't have one!

13:23.260 --> 13:25.930
I just want to be
less embarrassing right now!

13:26.013 --> 13:28.182
I want to say, "I made one too! I did it!"

13:42.279 --> 13:44.365
Well, look who it is. Hwang Dong-man!

13:47.701 --> 13:51.080
I wanted to sue you,
but you deleted all your online posts.

13:51.664 --> 13:53.165
You really want to debut, huh?

13:55.793 --> 13:56.752
Hey, did you know?

13:58.045 --> 14:02.258
If I hadn't brought over Ma Jae-yeong,
you wouldn't be debuting.

14:02.341 --> 14:06.095
Who knew I'd play the biggest role
in getting Hwang Dong-man to debut?

14:06.804 --> 14:08.722
Life is ironic, isn't it?

14:09.390 --> 14:11.058
Everyone's placing bets

14:11.141 --> 14:14.603
on whether you can see this to the end.

14:14.687 --> 14:16.689
There's a huge betting pool now.

14:17.982 --> 14:19.817
Don't flop too fast, though.

14:19.900 --> 14:21.694
You should at least make it fun
for those watching.

14:21.777 --> 14:23.028
Drive safely.

14:23.112 --> 14:24.154
Thanks, I will.

14:25.406 --> 14:26.824
Hold out as long as possible!

14:26.907 --> 14:28.075
So we can have fun watching!

14:28.617 --> 14:30.077
Good luck, Hwang Dong-man!

14:51.974 --> 14:53.142
CONGRATS ON YOUR DEBUT!

15:10.826 --> 15:11.911
Blow it out.

15:16.332 --> 15:17.666
Congratulations.

15:21.712 --> 15:22.755
What did you wish for?

15:25.174 --> 15:26.008
I just

15:26.884 --> 15:28.052
wished for forgiveness.

15:30.512 --> 15:32.139
I couldn't wish for success

15:32.890 --> 15:34.308
because I've committed too many sins.

15:35.517 --> 15:37.102
So I thought I should repent first.

15:44.234 --> 15:45.277
I can't do this.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.738
I can't keep it in, so I'll just tell you.

15:48.238 --> 15:49.740
When Jun-hwan was shooting his debut film,

15:49.823 --> 15:52.284
he called me in the middle of the night
and sobbed.

15:52.910 --> 15:54.036
And I got excited.

15:54.662 --> 15:55.537
I thought,

15:57.081 --> 15:57.957
"It finally got scrapped."

16:01.460 --> 16:02.419
I want to atone.

16:02.503 --> 16:04.171
I want to atone so badly.

16:04.755 --> 16:06.966
They all worked so hard
to get to where they are

16:07.049 --> 16:08.926
with such desperate determination.

16:09.677 --> 16:11.679
I sincerely want to apologize.

16:14.098 --> 16:16.809
Dear God, please forgive me.

16:17.685 --> 16:18.560
Please…

16:19.144 --> 16:20.104
Please…

16:20.896 --> 16:23.315
I'm so sorry, Jun-hwan.

16:24.984 --> 16:28.404
I thought getting a film greenlit
would be all I needed.

16:29.113 --> 16:30.030
I must be crazy.

16:30.114 --> 16:31.281
Why am I not happy?

16:31.907 --> 16:33.784
Two voices inside me are going wild.

16:33.867 --> 16:35.703
"I'm debuting! I'm so excited!"

16:35.786 --> 16:36.870
"This is bad."

16:37.538 --> 16:38.998
"Run away quickly."

16:39.081 --> 16:40.541
"Hurry, run away!"

16:41.583 --> 16:43.210
I have to kill off one of them.

16:44.003 --> 16:45.671
But how?

16:47.715 --> 16:50.926
What I dreaded the most
was being asked what I had filmed.

16:51.010 --> 16:52.386
But yay for me!

16:52.469 --> 16:54.221
Now I have something to say.

16:54.304 --> 16:57.766
Then I wonder,
"What if I can't see this through?"

16:57.850 --> 16:59.643
"I've never led anything in my life,

16:59.727 --> 17:02.187
so how can I lead 200 people?"

17:02.271 --> 17:03.188
"I can't do it."

17:03.272 --> 17:05.566
"I need to quit
before I make a fool of myself!"

17:05.649 --> 17:07.109
"Shut up, I'm doing this!"

17:10.904 --> 17:12.656
It'll be incredibly scary.

17:14.825 --> 17:16.076
But I'm even more afraid…

17:19.121 --> 17:20.289
of looking pathetic

17:21.457 --> 17:22.791
if I admit I'm scared.

17:38.640 --> 17:39.808
Don't worry.

17:41.727 --> 17:45.773
If you want to run away,
I'll do whatever it takes to help you.

17:48.275 --> 17:50.486
Fear isn't something you endure.

17:51.361 --> 17:53.072
You can't endure it.

17:54.031 --> 17:56.909
What kind of reward
justifies putting up with that?

17:58.869 --> 18:00.162
I won't let you go through that.

18:06.293 --> 18:07.377
When I was young…

18:10.297 --> 18:12.674
there was only one reason

18:13.383 --> 18:14.468
I wanted to grow up.

18:17.304 --> 18:19.181
So I could leave at any time.

18:21.934 --> 18:24.311
So I wouldn't have to endure
going through hell.

18:26.772 --> 18:30.359
My heart would pound so hard
that I couldn't even tell where it was.

18:32.986 --> 18:34.988
But I went to school
like nothing happened,

18:36.865 --> 18:38.033
ate alone,

18:39.701 --> 18:40.702
and slept alone.

18:43.455 --> 18:44.414
I used to feel

18:45.999 --> 18:46.959
that kind of fear.

18:49.128 --> 18:51.255
But I won't let you go through that.

19:19.825 --> 19:21.743
If you want to run away together,

19:23.036 --> 19:24.955
I'll run away with you.

19:26.874 --> 19:28.876
If you want to live in hiding forever,

19:30.252 --> 19:31.879
I'll hide with you.

19:36.717 --> 19:37.634
I like that.

19:53.650 --> 19:55.819
I'm such a lunatic.

19:56.445 --> 19:58.030
Even now,

19:58.113 --> 20:00.908
I'm still thinking about
my acceptance speech.

20:01.825 --> 20:02.743
Give your speech now.

20:03.744 --> 20:04.912
You need to practice.

20:04.995 --> 20:05.829
Come on.

20:07.873 --> 20:08.707
Ready.

20:09.333 --> 20:10.459
Action.

20:11.293 --> 20:15.672
The 2027 Korean Film Awards
Best New Director Award goes to…

20:16.465 --> 20:18.091
Drumroll, please.

20:18.675 --> 20:22.304
Hwang Dong-man for Weather Maker!

20:40.864 --> 20:43.367
I imagined the moment I would stand here

20:44.952 --> 20:46.411
every single day.

20:47.663 --> 20:49.831
And I finally made it.

20:53.710 --> 20:55.504
I want to say this to my friends.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.382
Congratulate me.

20:59.967 --> 21:01.176
Just congratulate me.

21:02.386 --> 21:04.054
I'm sorry I felt sick with jealousy…

21:06.014 --> 21:07.516
every time your films got greenlit.

21:08.267 --> 21:09.893
I'm sorry I felt happy

21:10.519 --> 21:12.145
every time they flopped.

21:12.896 --> 21:14.398
But just congratulate me.

21:15.190 --> 21:17.442
Congratulate me from the heart.

21:20.445 --> 21:21.613
Congratulations!

21:22.572 --> 21:23.949
Congratulations!

21:26.910 --> 21:27.744
And…

21:29.913 --> 21:30.831
to Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

21:34.501 --> 21:35.794
If it hadn't been for you…

21:38.088 --> 21:41.383
I wouldn't be standing here right now.

21:44.177 --> 21:45.220
Thank you.

22:19.629 --> 22:21.256
Now that I think about it,

22:21.340 --> 22:23.717
it wasn't half as scary as I had imagined

22:25.552 --> 22:28.013
when people found out I was unemployed.

22:30.515 --> 22:31.475
Maybe fear

22:31.558 --> 22:33.727
is only in our imagination.

22:33.810 --> 22:35.896
When you actually face it,
it might not be so scary.

22:39.649 --> 22:41.151
Whenever you feel scared,

22:42.527 --> 22:44.780
imagine that you're the guy next door.

22:46.990 --> 22:49.659
If the guy next door is in your situation,

22:50.619 --> 22:51.995
you'll think, "It's not a big deal."

22:54.456 --> 22:56.166
Other people's problems
are never a big deal.

23:03.215 --> 23:05.425
I'd like to cautiously offer a suggestion.

23:06.093 --> 23:07.636
What if your younger self

23:08.720 --> 23:09.971
was the kid next door?

23:12.057 --> 23:12.891
Would it help you

23:13.975 --> 23:16.144
let go of your fear a bit?

23:21.149 --> 23:23.318
If the kid next door
was going through that…

23:26.905 --> 23:28.573
I'll have to take them in.

23:38.542 --> 23:39.668
Ms. Ga Su-ja?

23:40.710 --> 23:41.962
-Yes?
-Please come in.

23:42.045 --> 23:42.879
Okay.

23:43.672 --> 23:45.507
There's really no need for this.

23:45.590 --> 23:46.842
Come on, get up.

23:48.093 --> 23:49.553
My goodness.

23:54.641 --> 23:57.269
WE SELL GIMBAP

23:57.352 --> 23:59.521
She's only getting her right knee done.

23:59.604 --> 24:01.231
It'll be a two-week hospital stay.

24:04.276 --> 24:06.486
You don't have to fly in.

24:06.570 --> 24:08.697
It's the end of the year,
so I bet things are busy at the store.

24:10.323 --> 24:12.993
Don't worry, Mom.
I have more money than you.

24:15.579 --> 24:17.080
I'm saying I have it because I do.

24:18.540 --> 24:20.667
Why would I take out a loan?

24:22.210 --> 24:25.255
The screenplay
still doesn't have a sharp feel to it.

24:25.839 --> 24:29.134
It seems the director prefers
an ending that lingers

24:29.217 --> 24:32.304
rather than a neatly resolved one.

24:32.387 --> 24:35.015
There's a difference
between lingering and incomplete.

24:36.391 --> 24:38.518
It feels like it could go further,
but it doesn't.

24:38.602 --> 24:40.061
Tell them to think it over again.

24:40.145 --> 24:41.521
Okay, I will.

24:41.605 --> 24:44.107
I'm not saying
it should be patched up with dialogue.

24:44.191 --> 24:45.317
There's already enough of that.

24:45.400 --> 24:46.234
Understood.

24:48.570 --> 24:51.698
I heard Choi Film got a good screenplay.

24:51.781 --> 24:52.824
Knock knock knock, was it?

24:53.450 --> 24:54.326
Bring it to me.

24:55.660 --> 24:59.080
But Mr. Noh Kang-sik
has already been cast for the role.

24:59.164 --> 25:00.332
I said bring it to me.

25:02.125 --> 25:02.959
Okay.

25:07.505 --> 25:10.467
Don't pay attention to anyone
accusing you of betrayal.

25:10.550 --> 25:13.511
If you make a hit, they'll disappear.

25:14.137 --> 25:16.681
If you're a pro,
you're forgiven for anything.

25:17.265 --> 25:18.099
Here you go.

25:19.267 --> 25:20.393
Let's make a blockbuster.

25:20.977 --> 25:21.978
Thank you.

25:22.062 --> 25:23.605
You know the title has to change, right?

25:23.688 --> 25:27.317
The screenplay is amazing,
but what's up with Knock knock knock?

25:27.400 --> 25:29.778
You don't get a title by mulling it over.

25:29.861 --> 25:31.529
It'll come out of nowhere one day.

25:31.613 --> 25:34.658
It'll raise its hand and yell,
"Here I am!" so don't worry about it.

25:36.284 --> 25:37.744
By the way, who's Yeong-sil?

25:38.912 --> 25:40.205
Your girlfriend?

25:40.288 --> 25:41.915
She's just

25:42.540 --> 25:43.625
a good friend.

25:43.708 --> 25:46.962
It felt like one person wrote it.
The flow and tone matched perfectly.

25:47.587 --> 25:48.755
You two should date.

25:50.006 --> 25:51.174
Not quite there yet?

25:52.467 --> 25:54.552
How much will Yeong-sil get paid?

25:55.595 --> 25:57.514
Has she signed a contract
with Kopark Film?

25:58.223 --> 25:59.391
No, not yet.

25:59.474 --> 26:01.268
Tell her I want to meet her.

26:01.851 --> 26:04.229
Tell her I'll sign her
for the highest fee in the industry.

26:05.105 --> 26:06.898
She'll be shocked at the amount.

26:07.941 --> 26:09.484
Oh, but the thing is,

26:10.694 --> 26:13.071
she doesn't like revealing herself.

26:14.030 --> 26:14.864
Why?

26:16.366 --> 26:17.784
Does she like being mysterious?

26:17.867 --> 26:19.911
She still has to sign the contract.

26:19.995 --> 26:22.622
Just tell her to meet me.
I'll treat her to an expensive meal.

26:26.668 --> 26:27.585
Is Yeong-sil

26:29.337 --> 26:31.047
under contract somewhere else?

26:32.841 --> 26:34.092
That was lovely.

26:34.175 --> 26:36.011
-It was a nice meal.
-Yes, I enjoyed it too.

26:40.307 --> 26:42.392
Hey, Ms. Ko. Fancy meeting you here.

26:45.770 --> 26:46.771
Hello.

26:47.564 --> 26:48.857
What did you have?

26:48.940 --> 26:49.774
Barbecue.

26:50.650 --> 26:52.694
You chose an expensive place to eat,
didn't you?

26:53.361 --> 26:54.779
I guess the KFA funds came through.

26:54.863 --> 26:56.156
I'm paying for it myself.

26:59.617 --> 27:01.494
You're so impulsive.

27:02.871 --> 27:04.789
Either swallow your pride
and stick with me,

27:04.873 --> 27:06.583
or just call it off completely.

27:07.250 --> 27:09.294
Why would you take on
Hwang Dong-man instead?

27:12.088 --> 27:12.922
You know, right?

27:13.006 --> 27:16.968
Byeon Eun-a,
who's known to revive dead screenplays,

27:17.052 --> 27:18.636
trashed that screenplay.

27:19.429 --> 27:20.764
I guess you haven't heard yet.

27:21.639 --> 27:24.225
That same Byeon Eun-a,
who's known to revive dead screenplays,

27:24.309 --> 27:26.227
helped review his screenplay.

27:28.355 --> 27:29.814
The revision turned out well.

27:30.440 --> 27:32.734
It's on a whole new level
from the one he submitted for the contest.

27:34.027 --> 27:36.404
If he had submitted this version,
he would've won.

27:37.030 --> 27:38.740
I'd love to see his film
open against Ma Jae-yeong's

27:38.823 --> 27:40.075
and see which one wins.

27:40.658 --> 27:42.369
Just tell him to see it through.

27:43.370 --> 27:45.080
Of course, he will.

27:45.163 --> 27:45.997
That's mine.

27:52.670 --> 27:53.505
Why are you hiding?

27:54.255 --> 27:55.840
A producer's career
depends on who they work with.

27:55.924 --> 27:57.300
You do whatever comes your way.

27:58.009 --> 28:00.678
Don't worry about it.
Just focus on your own work.

28:01.638 --> 28:03.390
I'll call you later!

28:15.151 --> 28:16.444
Hey, Ax.

28:21.616 --> 28:22.784
Why don't you just…

28:25.328 --> 28:26.454
go to Kopark Film?

28:26.538 --> 28:28.498
Be the producer for Hwang Dong-man's film.

28:29.124 --> 28:32.585
Go and worry about
whether you'll get paid on time,

28:32.669 --> 28:34.504
and spend your entire career there.

28:34.587 --> 28:35.797
You get your paychecks from me,

28:35.880 --> 28:37.841
but go around giving feedback
on other screenplays.

28:37.924 --> 28:39.008
You're a real headache.

28:40.385 --> 28:43.388
Critiquing screenplays
doesn't make you a producer.

28:44.013 --> 28:45.265
Do you want to be a writer?

28:45.348 --> 28:46.683
Are you doing this
because you want to write?

28:46.766 --> 28:49.185
I've seen countless producers quit

28:49.269 --> 28:51.730
and spend years struggling to write,

28:51.813 --> 28:53.481
only to return in the end.

28:54.274 --> 28:55.984
It's easy to criticize
other people's writing.

28:56.067 --> 28:57.318
Try writing something yourself!

29:00.488 --> 29:03.575
If I hear you're helping someone
with their screenplay again,

29:04.409 --> 29:05.452
it won't end well.

29:07.078 --> 29:08.037
Oh jeez.

29:09.330 --> 29:10.498
Do we have indigestion meds?

29:27.515 --> 29:28.767
MA JAE-YEONG

29:28.850 --> 29:31.269
We'll be signing
a writer's contract with Choi Film,

29:31.352 --> 29:32.645
so find someone to front it for you.

29:52.040 --> 29:53.875
-Wow, she's so pretty.
-She's like a doll.

29:54.542 --> 29:55.794
Isn't that Jang Mi-ran?

29:55.877 --> 29:57.629
-It is.
-No way.

30:02.300 --> 30:03.718
It's been a year since we filmed it.

30:03.802 --> 30:05.386
How am I meant to remember
how I felt then?

30:05.470 --> 30:08.932
Oh, there's no pressure.
You can just say what comes to mind.

30:10.016 --> 30:11.601
Dramas aren't good if you sit on them.

30:11.684 --> 30:15.146
They feel like leftover stock
that has lost its appeal.

30:15.230 --> 30:17.398
I wouldn't say we sit on them.

30:17.482 --> 30:19.108
A lot of work
goes into post-production, so…

30:19.192 --> 30:21.402
You're the only ones
who'd know the details.

30:21.486 --> 30:23.363
The average viewer has no idea.

30:24.823 --> 30:27.700
I liked it better when we shot
and aired it right away.

30:31.663 --> 30:33.957
-Hello!
-Oh, hey.

30:34.040 --> 30:36.668
-How are you doing, sir?
-How long has it been?

30:37.669 --> 30:38.503
Hello.

30:38.586 --> 30:39.754
-Take a seat.
-Hello.

30:39.838 --> 30:40.797
Hello.

30:43.383 --> 30:45.677
-It's been a while, Mi-ran.
-Yeah, it has.

30:48.388 --> 30:49.764
So we're going to ask you

30:49.848 --> 30:52.559
to share some moments
you remember from the shoot

30:52.642 --> 30:55.019
and what you will do for the fans
if it hits the streaming charts.

30:56.062 --> 30:59.899
I want everyone here
to love anyone this winter.

31:01.276 --> 31:05.780
The director said that you two
had such strong chemistry

31:05.864 --> 31:07.699
that it made him wonder
if you were really in love.

31:07.782 --> 31:08.783
Can you elaborate on that?

31:09.701 --> 31:12.537
Oh, my seven-year relationship
is still going strong.

31:14.539 --> 31:17.876
Honestly, my character is way more lovable
than I am in real life.

31:17.959 --> 31:20.169
Some lines made me wonder
how one could say such things to a woman.

31:20.753 --> 31:23.548
Personally, I found it
a bit embarrassing at first,

31:23.631 --> 31:26.509
but once I got into it,
I found it oddly satisfying.

31:26.593 --> 31:28.636
I even got carried away later on.

31:29.596 --> 31:32.557
I think people appreciated me
really committing to it.

31:32.640 --> 31:33.641
Thank you.

31:34.267 --> 31:36.227
Let's move on to the next question.

31:46.154 --> 31:46.988
Hello?

31:47.071 --> 31:48.865
It looks like you betrayed me.

31:48.948 --> 31:51.117
I heard you dropped out
of Director Lee Jun-hwan's film.

31:52.577 --> 31:54.412
Let's meet up.

31:57.415 --> 31:59.792
Why are there so many rom-coms
in South Korea?

31:59.876 --> 32:02.879
I don't think love is a good emotion.

32:02.962 --> 32:04.839
Being in love means you're crazy.

32:04.923 --> 32:06.549
You're not in your right mind.

32:06.633 --> 32:09.177
Is there anything good
about falling in love? No.

32:09.260 --> 32:11.429
Do you like being in love
with Hwang Dong-man?

32:12.013 --> 32:13.473
That's not love. That's support.

32:13.556 --> 32:14.891
Supporting someone is good.

32:20.104 --> 32:21.731
Damn it.

32:21.814 --> 32:24.025
Love from viewers, my ass.

32:24.817 --> 32:27.070
I'd settle for them not talking trash.

32:27.153 --> 32:28.529
Actors seem pretty tough, right?

32:28.613 --> 32:30.823
We have really low self-esteem.

32:30.907 --> 32:32.951
We're just people waiting to be used.

32:33.534 --> 32:36.621
No matter how much we want to work,
we have to be chosen to do so.

32:36.704 --> 32:38.373
It's not something we can do on our own.

32:38.456 --> 32:42.377
That's why we spend time alone,
drawing and making things.

32:43.044 --> 32:44.337
It's the same with producers.

32:44.963 --> 32:46.506
We can't do anything on our own.

32:47.882 --> 32:49.968
Writers seem like they've got it good.

32:50.051 --> 32:51.302
They can start whenever,

32:51.386 --> 32:53.429
and everything they write
becomes their asset.

32:53.513 --> 32:55.848
Why don't you become a writer?
You're good at reviewing screenplays.

32:55.932 --> 32:59.102
Being a good reviewer
doesn't make you a good writer.

33:00.186 --> 33:01.354
But…

33:02.522 --> 33:04.232
I'm good at reviewing and writing.

33:05.775 --> 33:06.859
You're so annoying.

33:07.610 --> 33:10.571
I didn't ask to meet you
so you could annoy me.

33:11.531 --> 33:13.324
My mind is just

33:13.408 --> 33:17.245
floating around
all over the place right now.

33:19.414 --> 33:21.416
But I don't want to
come back down to earth.

33:23.918 --> 33:25.962
But I might want to at some point,

33:26.045 --> 33:28.297
so I'm keeping my control tower
right here.

33:28.381 --> 33:29.757
Can I get another beer?

33:30.425 --> 33:31.384
Yes, ma'am.

33:31.467 --> 33:33.386
Hey, isn't that Jang Mi-ran?

33:34.887 --> 33:36.889
I think you're right. The cringe acting.

33:40.768 --> 33:41.602
Hey!

33:42.520 --> 33:45.064
I'm way fucking past
my cringe-acting days.

33:45.148 --> 33:46.649
Why are you still going on about that?

33:47.650 --> 33:49.986
-Watch my drama that airs tomorrow!
-No, no, no.

33:50.945 --> 33:52.822
Let's go get some fresh air.

33:52.905 --> 33:54.490
-Watch it and see if my acting is cringe!
-I'm sorry.

33:54.574 --> 33:57.035
-It's called I'll Love Anyone This Winter!
-I'm sorry.

33:57.118 --> 33:58.244
It's winter, you assholes!

33:58.327 --> 33:59.495
Get busy falling in love

33:59.579 --> 34:01.289
-instead of drinking around!
-Let's get some fresh air.

34:06.252 --> 34:08.713
I thought the life of a star
would be different.

34:11.716 --> 34:16.012
Someone once asked
what life as a star was like,

34:16.888 --> 34:18.431
and Oh Jeong-hui said,

34:19.390 --> 34:22.310
"It's the same as yours,
but without the money struggles."

34:23.770 --> 34:24.979
I just have a bit more money.

34:26.314 --> 34:27.648
Everything else is the same.

34:28.900 --> 34:31.694
It all sucks.

34:36.949 --> 34:38.868
To be honest, I can't act.

34:41.245 --> 34:43.456
The second I say "I love you,"

34:44.832 --> 34:47.168
I actually start having those feelings.

34:48.336 --> 34:51.005
Just like how I couldn't use my arm
after that scene where I cut it off.

34:53.800 --> 34:55.218
When I say "I love you"…

34:57.512 --> 34:59.097
I actually fall in love.

35:01.182 --> 35:02.058
Passionately.

35:07.230 --> 35:08.064
But guess what?

35:11.734 --> 35:13.277
That jerk said he was just acting.

35:18.407 --> 35:20.952
How could all of that
have just been acting?

35:24.956 --> 35:26.415
How could

35:27.625 --> 35:28.918
all of that…

35:32.004 --> 35:33.673
have just been acting?

35:37.844 --> 35:39.846
I get so upset that I wake up
in the middle of the night.

35:43.850 --> 35:45.935
After finishing a project,

35:47.019 --> 35:49.063
I feel like I've been covered in filth,

35:50.898 --> 35:53.151
like I've been used up and thrown away.

36:10.334 --> 36:11.669
This isn't good.

36:18.968 --> 36:20.469
I'm starting to like you.

36:52.960 --> 36:54.962
BY MA JAE-YEONG, YEONG-SIL

37:04.680 --> 37:06.849
If all people were born
from a bamboo shoot…

37:06.933 --> 37:08.100
I wish I had been born

37:08.184 --> 37:09.852
-from a bamboo shoot.
-…and there's no one to blame…

37:10.853 --> 37:13.731
She looks like
she's fed on fear her entire life,

37:14.690 --> 37:15.524
like a mass of fear.

37:15.608 --> 37:16.734
When I look at the streets,

37:17.860 --> 37:19.862
I don't see people walking.

37:20.571 --> 37:22.865
I see masses of emotion walking around.

37:24.909 --> 37:26.035
That's why…

37:26.118 --> 37:26.953
People are all…

37:27.036 --> 37:28.621
I don't see them as people,

37:28.704 --> 37:30.957
-…masses of emotion.
-but as masses of emotion.

37:31.040 --> 37:33.751
PEOPLE ARE ALL… MASSES OF EMOTION

37:48.349 --> 37:49.809
Are my thoughts the real me?

37:50.434 --> 37:51.435
Or is my body the real me?

37:52.561 --> 37:53.562
Mom.

37:54.438 --> 37:56.524
Are my thoughts the real me,
or is my body the real me?

37:57.566 --> 38:00.027
My thoughts can go anywhere

38:00.111 --> 38:01.529
and do anything.

38:01.612 --> 38:04.240
My thoughts can do everything,
so isn't that the real me?

38:11.914 --> 38:12.748
Knock knock knock

38:13.833 --> 38:14.792
is good.

38:18.129 --> 38:18.963
CEO CHOI DONG-HYEON

38:19.046 --> 38:20.006
Isn't it amazing?

38:21.299 --> 38:23.175
Who's Yeong-sil?

38:23.801 --> 38:25.052
It sounds like a pseudonym.

38:26.637 --> 38:29.557
I don't know yet.
They want to remain anonymous.

39:07.428 --> 39:09.722
TRAITS OF A VILLAIN…
SOMETHING SCARY…

39:16.520 --> 39:18.189
Who's your top choice?

39:19.148 --> 39:20.024
Noh Kang-sik.

39:22.026 --> 39:23.402
I just threw it out there.

39:24.570 --> 39:25.488
Let's give it a shot.

39:26.447 --> 39:27.615
What's there to lose?

39:36.791 --> 39:38.918
LOAN SHARK

39:44.298 --> 39:45.132
Hello?

39:45.216 --> 39:47.009
You fucking piece of shit!

39:47.093 --> 39:48.094
Hey, asshole!

39:56.936 --> 39:57.937
You know,

39:58.437 --> 40:01.941
my favorite thing in the world
is hearing you type.

40:03.025 --> 40:05.778
Clickety-clack, clickety-clack.

40:08.447 --> 40:09.573
I'm sorry.

40:09.657 --> 40:11.158
I wrote terribly, didn't I?

40:11.909 --> 40:13.702
I'll do better.

40:16.414 --> 40:18.207
I read Dong-man's screenplay.

40:19.542 --> 40:21.377
Oh, I guess it's good.

40:22.211 --> 40:24.463
Don't worry. Ours will be much more fun.

40:24.547 --> 40:26.465
Then what's with the crappy writing?

40:28.259 --> 40:31.053
I know you'll do well, Director Park.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.472
I'm just going to ride on your coattails.

40:34.765 --> 40:37.017
I've been really into
singing in a choir lately,

40:37.101 --> 40:39.645
and I actually cried on my first day.

40:40.229 --> 40:43.065
I barely opened my mouth,
yet beautiful sounds came out.

40:43.149 --> 40:46.026
Then I realized,
"Oh, I can just ride on their coattails."

40:46.110 --> 40:47.736
"There's happiness in that too."

40:49.321 --> 40:51.365
So I'm going to ride on your coattails.

40:51.991 --> 40:56.370
No matter what anyone says, to me,
you're the best writer in the world

40:56.454 --> 40:59.331
as well as the funniest and smartest.

41:08.716 --> 41:10.092
Your coattail-riding skills

41:11.135 --> 41:11.969
are exceptional.

41:17.266 --> 41:19.143
Looks like I'm writing the script, right?

41:19.226 --> 41:20.853
I'm just typing whatever.

41:21.729 --> 41:22.855
Just keep typing.

41:23.647 --> 41:25.232
-"Just keep typing."
-Something will come out.

41:25.900 --> 41:27.485
The sound of the keyboard
wakes up my brain.

41:28.777 --> 41:30.696
Don't think. Let your hands type.

41:31.280 --> 41:32.406
It's coming out.

41:32.990 --> 41:34.867
It's coming out.

41:34.950 --> 41:37.077
-It's coming out.
-It's coming out!

41:37.161 --> 41:39.246
I'm writing, I'm writing.

41:39.330 --> 41:40.623
Hey, I'm writing something!

41:40.706 --> 41:41.999
I'm typing, I'm typing.

41:42.875 --> 41:46.253
It's hard to get started, but once you do…

41:46.337 --> 41:47.546
Here we go!

41:47.630 --> 41:51.050
Don't think. Just let your hands type.

41:51.133 --> 41:53.552
Just a bit more.

41:53.636 --> 41:56.388
Hey! I'm writing, I'm writing!

41:56.472 --> 42:01.477
It's hard to start the engine,
but once it starts…

42:02.645 --> 42:04.146
I'm out of a crisis.

42:06.023 --> 42:07.149
I was so relieved

42:07.816 --> 42:10.778
to hear Gyeong-se would have a co-writer.

42:11.820 --> 42:13.030
You already know

42:13.697 --> 42:16.200
that all the women in his movies are you.

42:17.117 --> 42:19.703
You were Yeong-suk
in The Lustful Bottle Opener,

42:19.787 --> 42:21.455
as well as Mi-rae in Decision to Stay.

42:22.289 --> 42:23.123
He's only ever seen

42:23.999 --> 42:24.959
Ko Hye-jin.

42:26.627 --> 42:30.589
He likes you, respects you,
loves you, and relies on you.

42:32.341 --> 42:34.134
Directors feed on people's lives,

42:34.843 --> 42:37.137
but he stuck to you like glue

42:37.221 --> 42:39.932
and spent his entire life
on just one woman.

42:40.683 --> 42:43.185
I thought it was hopeless
unless he met another woman.

42:43.811 --> 42:44.728
It's such a relief

42:46.021 --> 42:47.648
that the woman is a writer.

42:49.233 --> 42:50.818
He won't be out fooling around.

42:51.777 --> 42:53.487
I won't complain
as long as the writing is good.

42:55.322 --> 42:56.740
Who cares what he does?

43:08.043 --> 43:09.336
This is it.

43:21.432 --> 43:22.808
Hey!

43:22.891 --> 43:25.769
Why did Oh Jeong-hui read the screenplay
I'm attached to?

43:29.982 --> 43:31.692
Go to Choi Film today
and sign the contract.

43:32.943 --> 43:34.236
Sign the contract!

43:35.362 --> 43:37.072
Before she pulls some weird stunt.

43:37.156 --> 43:38.115
I'm hanging up.

43:39.908 --> 43:41.744
What a load of crap.

43:42.786 --> 43:44.204
You know, right?

43:45.456 --> 43:48.042
My Mother was originally My Father.

43:48.125 --> 43:49.209
It was offered to me.

43:49.293 --> 43:52.046
But she persuaded the director
to change it to a female role,

43:52.129 --> 43:55.299
only to have it tank
after barely reaching six million.

43:55.382 --> 43:58.510
If I had done it,
I guarantee it would've hit ten million.

43:58.594 --> 44:00.220
Man, that damn woman…

44:00.888 --> 44:02.514
She did the same thing when she debuted.

44:02.598 --> 44:04.642
You know the story, right?

44:04.725 --> 44:06.810
She went in to audition
for the role of the female lead's friend,

44:07.394 --> 44:09.021
but instead performed
the female lead's lines.

44:10.272 --> 44:12.608
She's got a habit of stealing from others.

44:12.691 --> 44:15.819
That's also how she got her husband,
you know.

44:15.903 --> 44:18.947
He was supposed to marry Moon Ju-ryeon,
but she broke them up.

44:19.948 --> 44:21.784
If she tries to
pull a stunt like that on me--

44:21.867 --> 44:23.952
-Let's get ready!
-Okay.

44:24.036 --> 44:25.204
Thank you.

44:25.287 --> 44:26.163
Thank you.

44:26.246 --> 44:27.206
Wait, your script.

44:27.289 --> 44:29.083
It's fine. I don't need it.

44:36.548 --> 44:37.383
Give it to me.

44:37.466 --> 44:38.342
Here.

44:40.636 --> 44:41.679
-Hello, sir.
-Hey.

44:44.598 --> 44:46.475
-Time for a beating.
-Okay.

44:48.143 --> 44:49.269
Assistant Director, let's do it.

44:49.353 --> 44:50.312
Lights out.

44:55.692 --> 44:56.527
Let's go.

44:56.610 --> 44:57.486
Quiet on set.

44:57.569 --> 44:58.695
Ready.

44:59.154 --> 44:59.988
Cue!

45:01.240 --> 45:02.157
You know,

45:03.200 --> 45:06.328
I'm pretty familiar
with the look in gamblers' eyes.

45:11.875 --> 45:13.627
Their minds aren't with them.

45:14.837 --> 45:15.879
They're somewhere else.

45:16.588 --> 45:18.048
They're impatient.

45:18.132 --> 45:19.007
You know why?

45:20.342 --> 45:21.635
Because they need to make it all back.

45:28.434 --> 45:29.393
You know what?

45:30.436 --> 45:32.438
That look in your eyes
hasn't come back yet.

45:33.856 --> 45:35.190
I guess it's time for a beating.

45:47.202 --> 45:48.078
Cut!

45:54.501 --> 45:56.044
-Are you okay?
-I'm okay, sir.

45:56.128 --> 45:57.713
-Sorry about that.
-It's okay.

45:58.714 --> 46:00.757
Okay, we'll go with this.

46:01.550 --> 46:03.135
"Okay, we'll go with this"?

46:05.637 --> 46:06.763
Director!

46:07.514 --> 46:08.682
Yes?

46:13.520 --> 46:14.897
It sounds to me that it's not okay,

46:14.980 --> 46:16.857
but you'll just go with it anyway.

46:18.233 --> 46:21.945
"This is probably the best you can do."

46:22.029 --> 46:24.490
"Trying again won't get us anywhere,

46:26.116 --> 46:27.034
so let's just stop."

46:28.577 --> 46:29.411
Is that it?

46:29.495 --> 46:31.330
No, that's not what I meant.

46:32.789 --> 46:33.749
Let's go again.

46:36.001 --> 46:36.960
Got it?

46:51.391 --> 46:52.267
I'm sorry.

47:16.750 --> 47:19.545
FRONT DOOR

47:33.016 --> 47:33.976
It's just makeup.

47:36.228 --> 47:38.063
My mind is a mess,

47:38.146 --> 47:39.773
but I look too normal,

47:41.024 --> 47:42.359
so I messed up my face

47:43.110 --> 47:43.944
to match my mind.

47:47.281 --> 47:48.532
Tell me you liked me.

47:49.700 --> 47:51.994
I don't care
if you hate or loathe me right now.

47:52.077 --> 47:53.161
Just be honest

47:54.246 --> 47:55.247
and say you liked me

47:56.498 --> 47:57.624
back then.

48:00.168 --> 48:03.338
How many times do I have to tell you
that I was just acting?

48:03.422 --> 48:04.381
Really?

48:06.258 --> 48:07.801
You're telling me
you're that good of an actor?

48:09.511 --> 48:11.054
Do you really think you're that good…

48:13.056 --> 48:14.016
at acting?

48:15.559 --> 48:17.311
I watched everything you were in.

48:17.394 --> 48:19.021
I even watched your debut work

48:19.104 --> 48:20.814
to see if you were just acting.

48:21.565 --> 48:24.026
I'd believe you if I had seen
that same look even once in any of them.

48:25.569 --> 48:27.112
But I didn't. Not once.

48:27.696 --> 48:28.989
It was real for you too.

48:29.072 --> 48:31.033
Of course, it was real.
I don't fake my acting.

48:31.116 --> 48:33.827
You can't help but feel emotions
when you act.

48:33.910 --> 48:37.664
When I do stabbing scenes,
a murderous impulse rises in me.

48:37.748 --> 48:39.041
Does that make me a murderer?

48:39.124 --> 48:41.376
You were affectionate toward me
off-camera too!

48:41.460 --> 48:43.420
Why did you drunk dial me?

48:43.503 --> 48:45.422
Why did you get in my car
on the last day of filming,

48:45.505 --> 48:47.341
sit there in silence, and then leave?

48:47.424 --> 48:49.176
Just report that crazy bitch!

48:49.259 --> 48:50.344
Come out here.

48:51.678 --> 48:53.347
Come out. I said come out!

48:53.430 --> 48:54.306
Hey.

48:54.389 --> 48:56.224
I said come out here!

48:56.308 --> 48:57.517
Just stop already!

49:00.562 --> 49:02.314
Tell him I'll talk to her

49:02.397 --> 49:04.107
and that it'll never happen again.

49:16.286 --> 49:18.121
Did you go see Jung Hyeon-u again?

49:20.374 --> 49:21.333
Cut it out.

49:23.710 --> 49:26.630
I told his people it won't happen again.

49:26.713 --> 49:29.591
Don't give them a reason
to report you as a stalker.

49:32.761 --> 49:34.680
My drama started. Are you not going to
watch this one either?

49:36.723 --> 49:37.891
Can't you just watch it?

49:38.558 --> 49:39.643
I did well this time.

49:39.726 --> 49:41.269
I don't even watch my own.

49:46.942 --> 49:49.194
I acted for real this time!

50:02.332 --> 50:03.291
It's acting.

50:04.376 --> 50:05.502
Don't do it for real.

50:06.211 --> 50:07.504
Just make it feel real.

50:36.116 --> 50:38.076
LOAN SHARK

50:44.458 --> 50:46.460
-Hello?
-You motherfucker.

50:46.543 --> 50:48.295
How dare you
not pick up my call right away?

50:48.378 --> 50:51.131
You fucking piece of shit.
I'll beat the shit out of you.

50:51.214 --> 50:54.593
If you've got money, pay me back first.
Why the hell are you ignoring me?

50:54.676 --> 50:56.928
You'd better send me
11.9 million won by today.

50:57.012 --> 50:59.639
If you don't,
I'll text everyone in your contact list

50:59.723 --> 51:02.267
all day and night, you motherfucker.

51:03.018 --> 51:04.019
Excuse me.

51:04.102 --> 51:06.897
I used to get really stressed out
whenever you called.

51:08.690 --> 51:10.609
I thought it was because I was scared,

51:12.444 --> 51:13.653
but it was because I was fed up.

51:13.737 --> 51:14.571
FED UP

51:15.155 --> 51:16.698
To be honest, the way you talk

51:17.365 --> 51:18.283
is outdated.

51:18.950 --> 51:19.951
It doesn't scare me at all.

51:20.035 --> 51:21.036
You little…

51:21.119 --> 51:22.662
Are you out of your mind, little fucker?

51:22.746 --> 51:24.331
You motherfucking piece of shit!

51:24.414 --> 51:26.708
Are you running your mouth
because you want to die?

51:26.792 --> 51:28.835
I'll slice your gut open,
rip out your organs,

51:28.919 --> 51:30.670
and make a fucking soup with them!

51:30.754 --> 51:33.423
I'll gouge your eyes out with a hook
and chew them up!

51:33.507 --> 51:34.966
I'll rip out all your intestines

51:35.050 --> 51:37.302
and lay them out
like a fucking red carpet!

51:37.385 --> 51:38.512
Excuse me.

51:39.346 --> 51:42.140
You've never ripped out organs
or gouged out eyes before, have you?

51:43.058 --> 51:45.143
What the fuck? You little bastard.

51:45.227 --> 51:48.480
They say cliché writing comes from
a lack of understanding of the world.

51:48.563 --> 51:52.818
When I see writing that's full of clichés,
I feel like killing someone.

51:52.901 --> 51:55.529
It makes me want to
smash their goddamn head with my phone.

51:55.612 --> 51:57.447
These so-called writers

51:57.531 --> 52:00.242
keep pumping out familiar crap,
and you're no different, you asshole.

52:00.325 --> 52:01.952
You scare people for a living,

52:02.035 --> 52:04.037
but you never stop to think about
what actually scares them.

52:04.120 --> 52:05.997
It's always the same thing
about ripping out organs

52:06.081 --> 52:07.165
and gouging out eyeballs.

52:07.249 --> 52:08.542
-Is that all you can do?
-You fucking asshole.

52:08.625 --> 52:10.252
-It's because of lazy bastards like you
-Shut up.

52:10.335 --> 52:12.379
that gangster movies in this country
are going downhill!

52:12.462 --> 52:14.673
-I said shut the fuck up!
-If you're going to leech off people,

52:14.756 --> 52:16.091
at least put in some effort!

52:16.675 --> 52:18.593
-Shut the hell up!
-And stop with the cliché bullshit!

52:18.677 --> 52:21.263
-Shut up! Shut up!
-Do you even know what "cliché" means?

52:21.346 --> 52:23.515
-Shut the hell up!
-Dig through that brain of yours, idiot!

52:23.598 --> 52:26.184
-Shut the hell up!
-It means you're lazy as hell!

52:26.268 --> 52:28.103
I actually want to feel scared!

52:28.186 --> 52:31.147
-To the point of pissing myself, asshole!
-You're dead.

52:31.773 --> 52:33.108
Stay right there.

52:33.191 --> 52:34.860
You'd better not be wearing a gold chain.

52:43.243 --> 52:44.244
Fucking hell.

52:45.996 --> 52:47.080
Goddamn it!

53:21.489 --> 53:22.407
Thank you.

53:41.593 --> 53:43.970
Come out, you fucking asshole.

53:47.182 --> 53:48.558
I said come out!

53:51.311 --> 53:52.771
Goddamn it!

53:52.854 --> 53:53.730
Calm down.

54:07.285 --> 54:08.328
Hey.

54:10.747 --> 54:12.666
Where's Hwang Dong-man, that motherfucker?

54:14.876 --> 54:16.461
Where is he?

54:17.420 --> 54:19.214
You fucking assholes, I'm ought to just--

54:25.553 --> 54:26.596
-You're bleeding.
-Shit.

54:26.680 --> 54:27.597
You're bleeding.

55:20.859 --> 55:25.113
I texted everyone in your contact list,
you fucking piece of shit.

55:25.196 --> 55:26.614
Go ahead and keep ignoring me.

55:26.698 --> 55:29.409
I'll keep harassing them
until you pay me back.

55:42.589 --> 55:44.424
This motherfucker, Hwang Dong-man,

55:44.507 --> 55:47.635
took 11.9 million won from me
and is now ghosting me.

55:47.719 --> 55:50.597
Brace yourselves because I'm going to
harass you day and night

55:50.680 --> 55:52.098
until I get my money back.

55:52.182 --> 55:53.099
What the heck?

55:54.309 --> 55:56.144
CALL THIS NUMBER IF YOU SEE HWANG DONG-MAN

55:57.395 --> 55:59.105
Goodness gracious.

55:59.939 --> 56:02.150
This is more entertaining
than most screenplays.

56:02.233 --> 56:04.319
He'll never complete a film at this rate.

56:06.154 --> 56:08.114
Good luck, Dong-man!

56:17.707 --> 56:19.334
He borrowed from a loan shark?

56:19.959 --> 56:21.753
Hwang Dong-man is really something.

56:26.424 --> 56:28.301
I had opened my front door for a bit

56:28.384 --> 56:29.886
when my cat slipped out.

56:31.971 --> 56:33.014
It got hit by a car

56:34.224 --> 56:36.226
and needed emergency surgery,

56:36.851 --> 56:39.854
but I had already maxed out
my credit card.

56:41.314 --> 56:42.273
I'm sorry.

56:48.321 --> 56:50.490
This is why I like you.

56:51.366 --> 56:53.701
A man who borrows from a loan shark
to save his cat.

56:55.954 --> 56:57.455
Don't worry about it.

56:57.539 --> 56:59.207
It'll take more than that to break you.

57:03.336 --> 57:06.089
Why are you always so good to me?

57:09.092 --> 57:10.426
Because you deserve it.

57:28.528 --> 57:30.155
5-MINUTE LOAN APPROVAL
NO COLLATERAL OR GUARANTOR REQUIRED

57:30.238 --> 57:31.156
LOANS

57:46.129 --> 57:47.922
The second you say something cliché,
it's over.

57:48.006 --> 57:49.632
"Eyeballs." "Guts."

57:50.467 --> 57:52.510
The second you start throwing around
words like that, it's over.

57:53.636 --> 57:55.346
You made a big mistake.

57:55.430 --> 57:57.432
Now that you've blasted my contacts,

57:57.515 --> 57:59.601
what's supposed to scare me
into paying you back?

58:00.643 --> 58:02.312
You should've been more careful.

58:03.730 --> 58:06.524
Did you know the chief investigator
at Mapo Police Station is in my contacts?

58:07.442 --> 58:08.735
He's my cousin.

58:08.818 --> 58:10.069
He said to bring you in.

58:12.780 --> 58:13.740
But right now,

58:14.574 --> 58:15.575
I need

58:16.409 --> 58:17.952
something scary.

58:18.620 --> 58:20.622
If you show me something really scary,

58:20.705 --> 58:21.539
you'll get ten million won.

58:22.790 --> 58:23.750
It's worth it for me.

58:23.833 --> 58:25.460
Out of everything you've experienced

58:26.294 --> 58:28.087
and everything you've done,

58:28.880 --> 58:30.340
I want you to tell me

58:31.716 --> 58:32.842
what the scariest thing was.

58:36.638 --> 58:37.472
Or…

58:38.973 --> 58:40.808
you can just scare me right now.

58:44.938 --> 58:45.772
Fuck!

58:48.608 --> 58:50.443
You people are scarier than we are.

58:51.778 --> 58:55.281
When we go to collect, you cut gas lines,
start fires, and swing kitchen knives.

58:55.740 --> 58:59.244
That's why we barge in with our shoes on.
So we can run away if we have to!

58:59.327 --> 59:01.746
We don't wear them inside to scare you!

59:03.623 --> 59:04.457
You really have nothing?

59:06.417 --> 59:07.919
It's your chance to make ten million won.

59:08.002 --> 59:09.045
Screw you.

59:12.966 --> 59:13.800
We're done, then.

59:13.883 --> 59:16.719
I borrowed 1.7 million won
and paid back 5 million won.

59:16.803 --> 59:17.637
That's triple the amount.

59:18.972 --> 59:20.598
If you keep calling or texting,

59:21.891 --> 59:25.019
I'm going to come at you
with everything I've got

59:25.103 --> 59:26.479
and end you.

59:27.814 --> 59:29.857
You were able to push around
the old Hwang Dong-man,

59:30.692 --> 59:32.110
but I'm not the same man anymore.

59:36.781 --> 59:38.491
As of today, we're done.

59:39.242 --> 59:40.118
Got it?

59:42.912 --> 59:43.997
We're done.

59:45.290 --> 59:46.124
Got it?

59:59.012 --> 01:00:00.138
How did you handle it?

01:00:00.805 --> 01:00:02.265
You sure you don't need money?

01:00:02.348 --> 01:00:03.391
Yeah, I'm good.

01:00:05.476 --> 01:00:09.689
By the way, do you want the villain
to be more evil or just stronger?

01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:10.607
What?

01:00:10.690 --> 01:00:12.900
Most people confuse evil with strength.

01:00:13.776 --> 01:00:15.612
Do I make him more evil
or make him stronger?

01:00:18.489 --> 01:00:19.324
Stronger.

01:00:20.241 --> 01:00:21.200
Okay, got it.

01:00:30.627 --> 01:00:31.919
There's no evil in me.

01:00:33.087 --> 01:00:33.921
But there is strength.

01:00:52.774 --> 01:00:54.567
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:01:13.378 --> 01:01:15.463
I heard you gave Noh Kang-sik
Hwang Dong-man's screenplay.

01:01:15.546 --> 01:01:16.839
Did you do that
because you think you've got a shot?

01:01:16.923 --> 01:01:18.049
Why do you keep pestering me?

01:01:18.883 --> 01:01:20.301
Hello!

01:01:20.385 --> 01:01:21.344
When will you ever shine

01:01:21.427 --> 01:01:22.929
if you hide behind a pseudonym?

01:01:24.514 --> 01:01:26.349
Did you learn how to laugh yesterday?

01:01:26.432 --> 01:01:28.351
We got the CCTV footage,

01:01:28.434 --> 01:01:29.686
so we'll be seeing you soon.

01:01:29.769 --> 01:01:31.020
Why did you write the protagonist as male?

01:01:31.104 --> 01:01:33.856
The screenplay would work just fine
with a female protagonist.

01:01:33.940 --> 01:01:36.859
This is the second time
he offered a role and took it back.

01:01:36.943 --> 01:01:39.028
-He beat up another one. Cha Jeong-min.
-It's okay. Sit down.

01:01:39.112 --> 01:01:41.698
Why not just work with me

01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:43.574
before you get canceled
for beating a junior?

01:01:44.617 --> 01:01:49.622
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
